<h2 class="h5 mt-4 mb-2">The web app</h2>
<ul class="text-body-secondary">
    <li><b>Sign in</b> with Discord — CalCrony only asks for your identity and server list, never your messages.</li>
    <li><b>Do everything here</b>: events (create, edit, delete, RSVP), polls, templates, notifications, availability grids, calendar linking, the ICS subscribe URL, and server and personal settings — each feature's web side is described under <a href="/docs#features">Features in depth</a>.</li>
    <li><b>One source of truth</b>: RSVP here and the Discord embed updates within about 15 seconds; RSVPs made in Discord show up here on the next page load (pages don't refresh themselves).</li>
    <li><b>Themes</b>: pick one of five under My settings — the choice follows your account across devices.</li>
    <li><b>Managers</b> get the Activity log, the CSV export, and the server settings page (default channel, timezone, native events, public calendar).</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4 mb-2">Good to know</h2>
<Callout Variant="CalloutVariant.Note">
    <b>Calendar subscriptions refresh on the calendar app's schedule, not ours.</b> The feed itself
    updates the instant an event changes, but Google Calendar re-fetches URL subscriptions only every
    12–24 hours (with no manual refresh); Apple Calendar and Outlook let you choose a faster
    interval. If a new event seems missing from your calendar, it's almost certainly waiting on the
    next fetch — opening the subscribe URL that <code>/link</code> gives you always shows the
    current feed.
</Callout>
<p class="text-body-secondary" style="max-width:66ch">
    When connecting Google Calendar you may see a <i>"Google hasn't verified this app"</i> screen —
    click <b>Advanced</b>, then <b>Continue</b>; the permission requested is free/busy only (see the
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>). If you ever see a 🔄 "needs to reconnect" badge,
    re-running <code>/calendar connect</code> or clicking Connect in My settings fixes it in seconds.
    Server lists are a snapshot from sign-in; the "re-sync servers" link in the sidebar refreshes
    yours instantly.
</p>
<p class="text-body-secondary" style="max-width:66ch">
    Stuck, or have an idea? Join the
    <a href="https://discord.gg/aEdYyZYgyV" target="_blank" rel="noopener">community Discord server</a> —
    a support forum, release announcements, and a playground channel where you can try every command live.
</p>

@code {
    // Fragment links inside the page must be written as "/docs#features", not "#features": a
    // fragment-only href resolves against <base href="/"> and the router would navigate to the
    // landing page. Blazor scrolls to the fragment on those in-page navigations itself; a FRESH
    // load of /docs#features (the README's link) needs the nudge below, because the browser's own
    // fragment scroll runs before the app has rendered the heading.
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender)
        {
            return;
        }

        var fragment = new Uri(Nav.Uri).Fragment;
        if (fragment.Length > 1)
        {
            await Js.InvokeVoidAsync("calcronyPage.scrollToFragment", fragment[1..]);
        }
    }
}
